QA5 M1. errors.Is with io.EOF does not remove a wrapper that is not a tracked
value: the Unresolved value under its Wrap may be io.EOF or anything else, so
the entry stays, possibly handled. The Concrete Type (the wrapper with a nil
field) is not io.EOF and stays too. (Run time: the wrapper holds
os.ErrClosed.)
-- args --
a.go:@t
-- stdout --
